<script module>
  import Demo from "$ui/components/Demo.abide"
  import CellPeekProbeDemo from "$ui/demos/caching/CellPeekProbeDemo.abide"
  import CellPendingProbeDemo from "$ui/demos/caching/CellPendingProbeDemo.abide"
  import CellRefreshingProbeDemo from "$ui/demos/caching/CellRefreshingProbeDemo.abide"
  import CellErrorProbeDemo from "$ui/demos/caching/CellErrorProbeDemo.abide"
  import CellWatchProbeDemo from "$ui/demos/caching/CellWatchProbeDemo.abide"
</script>

<main class="page">
  <h1>Reactive probes</h1>
  <p class="lead">Every <a href="/caching/cell">cell</a> exposes the same reactive read surface — the <strong>probes</strong>. They are views of one slot's state machine (<em>idle → pending → value | error</em>, with a <code>refreshing</code> flag over a retained value). Because RPC and sockets ARE cells, this identical vocabulary shows up on <a href="/rpc/probes">RPC reads</a> and <a href="/sockets/probes">sockets</a> too — here each probe runs over a plain client-side <code>cell()</code>, one demo apiece.</p>

  <h2><code>peek()</code> — the non-blocking snapshot</h2>
  <p><code>undefined</code> while the first load is in flight, the value once it resolves. Reading it subscribes the caller and kicks a coalesced load.</p>
  <Demo id="cell-peek" title="<code>cell.peek(args)</code>" client="src/ui/demos/caching/CellPeekProbeDemo.abide" tab="client">
    <CellPeekProbeDemo />
  </Demo>

  <h2><code>pending()</code> — the first-load flag</h2>
  <p><strong>yes</strong> only while the first load runs (no value yet); back to <strong>no</strong> once the slot settles.</p>
  <Demo id="cell-pending" title="<code>cell.pending(args)</code>" client="src/ui/demos/caching/CellPendingProbeDemo.abide" tab="client">
    <CellPendingProbeDemo />
  </Demo>

  <h2><code>refreshing()</code> — revalidation over a retained value</h2>
  <p>Distinct from <code>pending</code>: <strong>yes</strong> only while a re-fetch runs over a value that stays on screen. Load, then refresh — the value holds, <code>refreshing</code> flips to yes, <code>pending</code> stays no.</p>
  <Demo id="cell-refreshing" title="<code>cell.refreshing(args)</code> vs <code>pending(args)</code>" client="src/ui/demos/caching/CellRefreshingProbeDemo.abide" tab="client">
    <CellRefreshingProbeDemo />
  </Demo>

  <h2><code>error()</code> — the retained error</h2>
  <p>A rejected load lands on the slot; <code>error()</code> holds it until an <code>invalidate</code> + successful read clears it.</p>
  <Demo id="cell-error" title="<code>cell.error(args)</code>" client="src/ui/demos/caching/CellErrorProbeDemo.abide" tab="client">
    <CellErrorProbeDemo />
  </Demo>

  <h2><code>watch(args, cb)</code> — the method form</h2>
  <p>Runs the callback whenever <em>this slot's</em> value changes (unlike <code>watch(thunk)</code>, which auto-tracks an expression). Every load and refresh fires it.</p>
  <Demo id="cell-watch" title="<code>cell.watch(args, cb)</code>" client="src/ui/demos/caching/CellWatchProbeDemo.abide" tab="client">
    <CellWatchProbeDemo />
  </Demo>
</main>
